Develop a Python-based pricing and risk management application that prices complex autocallable notes (e.g., worst-of Phoenix autocalls linked to a multi-asset equity basket). The engine simulates underlying asset paths using advanced stochastic models (Heston Stochastic Volatility) to properly capture the volatility skew and smile. It evaluates path-dependent early redemption and coupon triggers across discrete observation dates, and outputs accurate prices alongside exact exotic Greeks (Delta, Vega).
